{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/figure-fields-2/PROBE-DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"# The figure fields, second version: empty unless the article says it. Probe design (D497), 2026-11-15\n\n**What it can decide.** Whether c22, which differs from the first arm (c21) only in the wording of the two field definitions, (1) leaves a\nfigure's source empty where the article states the figure in its own voice, (2) writes a fixed period only where the article writes that\nyear, (3) keeps the first arm's gain (the market's figure and the company's figure under their own names), (4) does not now empty a\nsource the article does state, and (5) leaves what the request decides today as it was. Read on ten stored states the first probe did\nnot use. A pass leads to the record test on unread articles, asked of Alex first; anything else stops the line and goes to him.\n\n**Alex's word (D497):** \"做第二版再测\", on the option \"把两个字段的定义改成“文章没明说就留空”，换另一批已存文章按同样的方法再测\".\n\n## Diagnosis first (the first arm's own stored reasoning, $0)\n\n- *The unattributed outlook.* On \"Gross margins are expected to bottom in the 71% to 72% range in Q4 …\" the reasoning of all three sends\n  calls it \"gross margin guidance\" at once and never asks whose expectation it is. Nothing in the first definitions named that case.\n- *The year never written.* On an article that writes only \"fiscal 2028\", one send worked the quarter's year out from the publication\n  date (which the definition forbade), two from \"the next year (fiscal 2028)\" (\"so current fiscal year is 2027\"). The first definition\n  said \"establishes\", which a deduction satisfies.\n\n## The candidate (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c22-*`)\n\nSystem text and closing check: c8's, byte for byte. Schema: c21's, with the two descriptions reworded (7,254 → 7,582 characters as sent):\n- `party`: the company is the source of its own reported result; of a forecast **only where the item says the company, its management or\n  a named executive gave it**; the named person, firm or \"consensus\" for analysts' or the market's expectation; the author or outlet for\n  its own calculation. \"A forecast the item states in its own voice without saying whose it is (\"margins are expected to fall\",\n  \"earnings are projected at\") has no stated source: party is null, and its kind is estimate, not guidance.\"\n  Source: the signed standard's rule that an unknown speaker stays unknown and an inference is not written as a source's statement\n  (council mx round 8); the existing definition of guidance as \"the company's own outlook\".\n- `fiscal_period`: a fixed form \"only when the item itself **writes the year** of this figure's period\", anywhere in the item for the\n  same period; null when the item never writes that year (\"a quarter or \"the full year\" with no year; a year that would have to be\n  worked out from another year the item mentions\"), for a range or a deadline, and never from the publication date or outside knowledge.\n  A choice of wording within Alex's shape (a period in a fixed form): the strict form is the one code can check, and an empty period\n  costs a grouping while a wrong one corrupts it. It gives up the correct deductions the first arm made (15 figures); that cost is\n  counted below.\n- The `kind` field's own description is c8's, untouched.\n\n## Cases (`cases-figure-fields-2.json`; stored c8 requests and states of the week, steps 13, 16, 33, 50, 55, 73, 98, 116, 231, 232)\n\n| case | step | what the article holds | what must come out |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| u1-target | 231 | \"The company's upcoming EPS is projected at $2.47\"; \"our latest consensus estimate expects the revenue to be $109.02 billion\"; the full-year Zacks consensus; no fiscal year written anywhere | the EPS: empty, or the outlet's consensus, not the company, and not guidance; the two consensus figures: the market's; every fixed period empty |\n| u2-target | 50 | \"Nvidia is expected to have earnings per share of $15.68\" for fiscal 2028 | empty or analysts, not the company; not guidance; FY2028 |\n| m1-target | 232 | \"Management guided revenue for that quarter to $108 billion\"; \"The consensus forecast for that quarter is $111.3 billion\" | the guide the company's (not empty); the consensus the market's |\n| m2-target | 16 | \"the company projected 70% … in fiscal 2028 — well above the 45% analysts had expected\"; margin \"sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter\" in analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg | 70% the company's; 45% and the margin estimate the analysts'; \"the fourth quarter\" and \"last quarter\" empty |\n| m3-target | 73 | \"Revenue in the second quarter of fiscal 2027 … was $96.2 billion\"; \"the consensus revenue estimate of $109.0 billion\" for the next report | the revenue the company's, FY2027-Q2; the estimate the market's |\n| a1-control | 98 | \"For fiscal 2028, management has guided about 70% revenue growth\"; \"the guide has that margin settling in the 72% to 73% range\" | both the company's, **not empty** (the guard against emptying what is stated) |\n| p1-target | 55 | the fiscal second quarter's results, \"roughly 70% revenue growth in the next fiscal year\", \"the current quarter\"; no fiscal year written anywhere | every fixed period empty; the parties the company's |\n| p2-target | 13 | \"latest quarter generated $89 billion of data-center revenue\"; no fiscal year written | every fixed period empty |\n| k1-keep | 116 | c8 opened the Hugging Face question here (stored draw) | |\n| k2-keep | 33 | c8 opened the Blackwell China question here (stored draw) | |\n\nBoth arms (c8, c22) on all ten, three sends each: 60 sends; about $0.90 (dry run $0.86; the first probe cost $0.85); ceiling $2.00.\nc21 is not sent again: its numbers on the first ten cases are the reference for what the rewording changes, on different articles.\n\n## Who reads (as the first probe, with its lessons)\n\nTwo blind reader families on two packets, the article shown with its title and publisher. Packet one (both arms, one shape, no fixed\nperiod): per figure the party (right / wrong / missing / unknown_ok), measure, value and kind; per statement its own party and date; the\nnamed figures' places; the links of the statements with figures on the eight target and control cases. Packet two (c22 only): per\nfigure, whether the article writes the year of its period, and the fixed period right / wrong / empty. **Packets go to the Codex readers\nin parts of ten answers.** Marks the families give differently are read again by a fresh reader of each family **for both arms**; a\nline those could still change is undecided. **Beside the readers, a code check** on the period rule, which is mechanical: for every\nfixed period c22 writes, the year in it must be written in the article with its fiscal or calendar marker; each failure is listed.\n\n## Counting (frozen before any send; rates over an arm's valid sends of a case; \"most\" is two thirds)\n\n- *Valid sends:* at least two of three per case and arm, or the case is left out for that arm and listed.\n- **Named figures** (each case's list, with its accepted and rejected sources; exercised when c22 keeps the figure in at least two valid\n  sends, and c22 must keep it in no fewer sends than c8 less one): right when, over the sends that keep it, the readers mark its party\n  right (or unknown_ok where the case accepts empty) in most, and, where the case says \"not guidance\", its kind is not guidance in most.\n  A case passes when every exercised named figure is right. **Line:** at least six of the eight target and control cases exercised, and\n  all exercised cases pass but at most one; a1-control must be exercised and pass (a stated source is not emptied).\n- **Party, all figures:** c22's parties wrong in no more than one in twenty after settling; missing counted apart: missing (empty though\n  the article says whose) in no more than one in ten.\n- **Fixed period:** by code, c22's fixed periods whose year the article does not write: no more than one in twenty of its figures, and\n  none in most sends of p1, p2 or u1. By the readers: where the article writes the year, c22's fixed period right in at least two thirds\n  (needs ten such figures) and wrong in no more than one in twenty. Reported: how many correct fixed periods the strict rule leaves\n  empty, against the first arm's share.\n- **Guards** (each fails the probe): openings on the keep cases (lower than c8's by two thirds in a case or by a half pooled; control\n  absent when c8 opens in fewer than most; reported per case, never as \"preserved\"); kept statements, statements linked to an open\n  question and figures per send, pooled, each not lower than c8's by more than a third; each statement-to-question link on the target and\n  control cases not \"most against none\" between arms unless both families call the difference right; the statement's own party and\n  date on the statements holding the named figures not wrong in more sends than c8's by two or more; measure and value wrong in no more\n  than one in twenty; kind wrong after settling in no more than one in twenty and not more than c8's rate plus one in twenty; invalid\n  sends no more than c8's plus one.\n- **The tally prints every line above with its verdict**; a line it cannot compute is reported as not computed, not as met.\n\n**Verdict:** inconclusive = a required condition not exercised; undecided = a difference the fresh pair leaves that could change a line;\npass = every line met; fail = anything else. **Stop:** anything but a pass stops the line and goes to Alex with the listing.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A 30 -B 3 'D496|D497' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"5674-  until a result is adopted. First a probe on stored states with guards on what the request decides today, its lines and stop written\n5675-  before any send and a council round before the send; then the record test on unread articles, only if the probe passes.\n5676-\n5677:## D496 · 2026-11-14 · The figure-fields arm (c21): the fields repair attribution, the probe is undecided and stops; the arm infers what articles imply (council consensus)\n5678-\n5679-- **Probe** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/figure-fields/PROBE-DESIGN.md`, `RESULT.md`; one blind audit of the wording and council rounds\n5680-  6 and 7 before the send): ten stored states, c8 and c21, three sends each, 60 valid sends, $0.85.\n5681-- **Result:** the party of the named figures is right in the four target cases that could be judged, where c8 fails all four (the market's\n5682-  45% under the CFO's name; the author's estimate under the company's; the reported 75% under the CFO's; the consensus under the\n5683-  company's); wrong parties over all figures 2.1% against c8's 8.2%. Kept, linked, opened, the statements' own fields and measure and\n5684-  value were not seen to move. **Undecided:** on one article that states figures in its own voice the arm gives them to the company as its\n5685-  outlook, which one reader family marks wrong and the other right, twice (kind wrong 2.6% settled, 5.1% or more by the strict reading);\n5686-  and it writes a fiscal year for 15 figures of one article that never writes that year, which both families let pass.\n5687-- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mx-codex-8.md`): \"Record the probe as undecided and stop; complete the frozen guard\n5688-  accounting and adjudicate the unattributed expectations against the existing source rules before framing a product choice. A\n5689-  favourable ruling on kind alone is insufficient to advance to the unread-article test.\" The accounting is completed in the result; by\n5690-  the signed standard (an unknown speaker stays unknown) the strict reading holds.\n5691-- **Decided:** c21 as written is not carried to the unread-article test. What the probe names is one behaviour, inference where the article\n5692-  is silent, at two fields. A second version of the two definitions that makes \"empty unless the article says it\" the rule would be a new\n5693-  candidate, read on other stored articles with this probe's method; its cost (about $0.90) goes to Alex first, since the test he opened\n5694-  was sized at about a dollar and that is spent.\n5695-\n5696:## D497 · 2026-11-15 · Alex approves a second version of the figure fields and its probe\n5697-\n5698:- **Asked** (after D496, his reply to this exact question): \"“每个数字自带来源”的测试结果是未决：新字段把之前安错的来源分对了（来源错误率从 8.2% 降到 2.1%），其他行为没变；但模型会替文章补全\n5699-  没明说的来源和财年，按严格读法有两项差一点没过线。我按规则停下了。要不要再花约 $0.9 做第二版？\" Options: a second version and another probe (recommended); stop here.\n5700-- **Alex:** \"做第二版再测 (Recommended)\". The option as shown: \"把两个字段的定义改成“文章没明说就留空”，换另一批已存文章按同样的方法再测，约 $0.9（累计将到约 $7.5）。通过后再问你要不要在没看过\n5701-  的文章上做记录测试。\"\n5702-- **Decided:** a second arm (c22) differing from c21 only in the wording of the two field definitions, so that a source or a fiscal year the\n5703-  article does not state stays empty; diagnosed first from the stored reasoning of the two behaviours; read on stored articles the first\n5704-  probe did not use, with the first probe's method and its lessons (a code check beside the readers where the rule is mechanical; both\n5705-  arms settled alike; the tally printing every line); the unread-article record test only after a pass, asked of him first.\n5706-\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
